Modifications
-------------
None. dataset/mlpromise_english.json is byte-identical to the file as released.

This study does normalise the data before use -- whitespace is stripped from
one label, row ids are derived from row content, and the labels are translated
into this study's own vocabulary -- but all of that happens at load time in
paper/data_en.py and paper/labels_en.py. The stored file is never rewritten, so
the recorded sha256 keeps meaning "what the authors published".


What is and is not covered
--------------------------
This notice covers dataset/mlpromise_english.json only.

Artifacts derived from it -- the fold manifests under splits_en/ and the
predictions written by paper/run_decisions.py -- carry row ids and labels but
none of the source paragraph text. The rest of this repository is independent
work collected alongside the dataset, not an adaptation of it.

Nothing here is legal advice. It records what was retrieved, from where, under
which licence, and what was changed, which is what the licence asks a
redistributor to state.
